  "gameDescriptionHtml": "\nMost people resort to therapy. But you chose the brave option. A sledgehammer.<p></p>\n<p>In Virtue and a Sledgehammer, explore the remains of your hometown haunted by the android ghosts of your digitized neighbors. There won’t always be a clear path, so create your own by knocking down any structures that stand in your way.</p>\n<p>It will be a painful journey, not only because of the assault from the robots that have taken over life in the mountains, but because of the memories you’ll unearth—sometimes warm, but often traumatic—as you destroy the remnants of your childhood.</p>\n<p>A game about family, traditions, and being a misfit.</p>\n<p>Wield your sledgehammer like an instrument of reckoning, swinging through the swathes of mechanical human facsimiles and the buildings they call home. But will violent catharsis salve your soul, or make the pain burn brighter?</p>\n<p>You can’t tear down the place you were born without awakening a few ghosts. The cinematic sequences of interactive fiction will reveal your fears, desires, and your family’s knotty web of virtues and flaws.</p>\n<p>Flesh is a source of aches and tainted humors.</p>\n<p>It’s only now, devoid of bones, devoid of hunger, that I can tell you…</p>\n<p>I have never been happier.<br>\n</p>",
